speechtext:
Motion No. 47
That Bill C-48, an act to regulate oil and gas interests in Canada lands and to amend the Oil and Gas Production and Conservation Act, be amended in Clause 56 by adding immediately after line 2 at page 49 the following:
"(6) Notwithstanding anything in this act, where the Minister proposes to make an order in respect to:
(a)	the granting of exploration agreements, leases, permits, special renewal
permits, and production licences;
(b)	declarations of significant discovery;
(c)	drilling of wells;
(d)	declarations of commercial discovery; and
(e)	the matters described in Section 48,
the aboriginal peoples affected by such an order shall be given reasonable notice by the minister through their authorized representatives."
